BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Arts & Humanities Institute
DTSTART:20261004T190000Z
DTEND:20261004T200000Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Art & a Movie at the Eskenazi Museum: Women Photographers with Sh
 anti Knight
DESCRIPTION:3:00-3:30 p.m. Martin Commons\, 2nd floor  Knight will presen
 t a talk exploring the contributions of women photographers throughout hi
 story. Drawing inspiration from themes raised in War Paint\, the lecture 
 will highlight the important role women have played behind the camera\, o
 ften in the face of significant barriers\, as well as women's current cha
 llenges and opportunities within the profession.3:30-4:00 p.m. "Ask Me An
 ything" conversation with Knight. She will share insights from her work a
 s the Eskenazi Museum of Art's photographer and reflect on her experience
 s as a full-time professional photographer.  After the program\, guests w
 ill receive a list featuring works by women photographers in the museum's
  collection and in The Photographic Reflex. From 4:00-5:00 p.m.\, visitor
 s are invited to explore the museum independently and spend time with the
 se artworks.Bio:Shanti Knight has been the photographer at Eskenazi Museu
 m of Art since 2019. She began working in the field as a teenager\, growi
 ng up in her father's photography business and starting her independent p
 ractice in her 20s. She earned her Bachelor of Arts in Journalism with a 
 Second Concentration in Fine Arts from Indiana University in 2011. She la
 unched her career in New York City with an internship at Glamour magazine
 . In the years following\, she has assisted\, shot for\, and received dir
 ect training and mentorship from more than 30 different professional phot
 ographers\, mostly high-end professionals in New York City and Chicago wi
 th a variety of specialties\, including\, but not limited to\, wedding\, 
 editorial\, fashion\, and commercial work\, and she has served clients fr
 om coast to coast.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="font-weight: 400\;"><strong>3:00-3
 :30 p.m. Martin Commons\, 2nd floor</strong></p><p style="font-weight: 40
 0\;">  Knight will present a talk exploring the contributions of women ph
 otographers throughout history. Drawing inspiration from themes raised in
  <em>War Paint</em>\, the lecture will highlight the important role women
  have played behind the camera\, often in the face of significant barrier
 s\, as well as women's current challenges and opportunities within the pr
 ofession.</p><p><strong>3:30-4:00 p.m.</strong> "Ask Me Anything" convers
 ation with Knight. She will share insights from her work as the Eskenazi 
 Museum of Art's photographer and reflect on her experiences as a full-tim
 e professional photographer.</p><p>  After the program\, guests will rece
 ive a list featuring works by women photographers in the museum's collect
 ion and in <em>The Photographic Reflex</em>. From 4:00-5:00 p.m.\, visito
 rs are invited to explore the museum independently and spend time with th
 ese artworks.</p><p><span data-markjs="true">Bio:</span><span data-markjs
 ="true">Shanti</span> Knight has been the photographer at Eskenazi Museum
  of Art since 2019. She began working in the field as a teenager\, growin
 g up in her father's photography business and starting her independent pr
 actice in her 20s. She earned her Bachelor of Arts in Journalism with a S
 econd Concentration in Fine Arts from Indiana University in 2011. She lau
 nched her career in New York City with an internship at <em>Glamour</em> 
 magazine. In the years following\, she has assisted\, shot for\, and rece
 ived direct training and mentorship from more than 30 different professio
 nal photographers\, mostly high-end professionals in New York City and Ch
 icago with a variety of specialties\, including\, but not limited to\, we
 dding\, editorial\, fashion\, and commercial work\, and she has served cl
 ients from coast to coast.</p>
