SUMMARY:Humanities Hangout with Rachel Whitney (IU B.A. '04\, Internation
 al Studies + Spanish)
DESCRIPTION:Full description:  Would you like to learn how your major or 
 minor in the humanities gives you important preparation that will help yo
 u in many different professional fields?  If so\, please join us for a Hu
 manities Hangout on Monday\, October 5\, at 4 pm in Maxwell Hall\, with R
 achel Whitney (IU B.A. '04\, International Studies + Spanish\; MBA\, Vand
 erbilt University).  Ms. Whitney will speak about how a humanities perspe
 ctive has influenced her approach to business\, problem solving\, decisio
 n making\, working with others\, and more.  Ms. Whitney has worked in mus
 ic in Nashville for 20 years. She has focused in particular on the inters
 ection of music and technology. She has worked at YouTube and Pandora and
 \, most recently\, has spent five years at Spotify as the Head of Editori
 al for Nashville\, where she led the team that covers rock and alternativ
 e\, country\, and Christian and gospel music programming. Before working 
 in music programming\, she was Director of Digital Marketing at Borman En
 tertainment. She currently serves on the board of the Americana Music Ass
 ociation and has also served on the boards of the Country Music Associati
 on and Leadership Music.  Come see how exploring your interests in the hu
 manities can help you prepare for a variety of careers!  Pizza will be se
 rved.  This series is presented by the College Arts + Humanities Institut
 e and the Department of Spanish and Portuguese. If you need assistance\, 
 or if you have questions about physical access\, please email cahi@iu.edu
  or call (812) 856-1169. Accommodations can be made to meet most needs.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Full description:</strong></p><p>
