BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Arts & Humanities Institute
DTSTART:20261020T180000Z
DTEND:20261020T200000Z
LOCATION:LILLY LIBRARY
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
SUMMARY:An ornithology pop-up exhibition
DESCRIPTION:Whether locally or globally\, birds are a critical part of Ea
 rth's ecosystems. This event is a celebration of birds as they appear in 
 historical books and manuscripts.  Visitors can page through the Lilly Li
 brary's dazzling collection of ornithology materials and learn how to get
  more involved in local bird conservation efforts. Visitors will have a c
 hance to get up close and personal with one of the great treasures of the
  Lilly Library—the Double Elephant Folio edition of John James Audubon'
 s Birds of America\, featuring life-sized\, hand-colored engravings of Au
 dubon's captivating ornithological studies. Indiana University's own Audu
 bon expert\, Dr. Christoph Irmscher\, will be present to talk about his r
 esearch and writings on Audubon and natural history.Larks\, Loons\, and L
 orikeets at the Lilly: An Ornithology Pop-Up Exhibition&#160\;is free and
  open to bird nerds of all ages.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  Whether locally 
 or globally\, birds are a critical part of Earth's ecosystems. This event
  is a celebration of birds as they appear in historical books and manuscr
 ipts.</p><p>  Visitors can page through the Lilly Library's dazzling coll
 ection of ornithology materials and learn how to get more involved in loc
 al bird conservation efforts. Visitors will have a chance to get up close
  and personal with one of the great treasures of the Lilly Library—the 
 Double Elephant Folio edition of John James Audubon's <em>Birds of Americ
 a</em>\, featuring life-sized\, hand-colored engravings of Audubon's capt
 ivating ornithological studies. Indiana University's own Audubon expert\,
  Dr. Christoph Irmscher\, will be present to talk about his research and 
 writings on Audubon and natural history.</p><p><em>Larks\, Loons\, and Lo
 rikeets at the Lilly: An Ornithology Pop-Up Exhibition</em>&#160\;is free
  and open to bird nerds of all ages.</p>
UID:20261020T180000Z-2417196@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260914T121647Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/birds-in-books
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925T162754Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop
 /1/src_region/0,0,600,600/32451_ornithology_pop-up_livewhale_avatar.rev.1
 789052157.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2417196
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/heig
 ht/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,600\,600/32451_ornithology_pop-up_livewhal
 e_avatar.rev.1789052157.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  <strong>Lilly Library</strong><br />\n  <
 a href="mailto:liblilly@iu.edu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">liblilly@i
 u.edu</a>\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">\n  Join us at IU Libraries
  Lilly Library on Tuesday\, October 20 from 2–4pm for <em>Larks\, Loons
 \, and Lorikeets at the Lilly: An Ornithology Pop-Up Exhibition</em> in p
 artnership with the Sassafras Audubon Society of Indiana!\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-RSVP:1
END:VEVENT
