SUMMARY:Theory Center Fall Symposium
DESCRIPTION:The Center for Theoretical Inquiry in the Humanities invites 
 you to a symposium on the thought of Martin Heidegger featuring guest sch
 olars Alberto Moreiras (Texas A&amp\;M) and Laurence Hemming (Lancaster U
 niversity and Director of Knapp Foundation). Join us in Global and Intern
 ational Studies Building 1060 for guest lectures from Moreiras and Hemmin
 g\, with discussion and a catered lunch to follow. After\, the event move
 s to Indiana Memorial Union's Oak Room\, where Moreiras and Hemming will 
 lead a workshop.  The workshop will provide an opportunity to discuss pre
 circulated papers by Moreiras and Hemming addressing themes close to Heid
 egger's concerns during the 1930s and beyond: capitalism and Gestell\; th
 e closure of metaphysics and ontological fatigue\; and homelessness and f
 reedom in existential and political contexts. Graduate students are stron
 gly encouraged to participate.Schedule of Events:9:00 - 9:15 amWelcome&#1
 60\;(GISB 1060)9:15 am - 12:30 pmPresentations by Alberto Moreiras (Texas
  A&amp\;M) and Laurence Hemming (Lancaster University)\, discussion to fo
 llow12:30 - 1:30 pmCatered lunch2:00 - 4:00 pmWorkshop (IMU Oak Room)
