 cable" data-linkindex="0">And So I Stayed</a></em>\, an a<span class="x_g
 mail_default">ward-winning</span> documentary about survivors of domestic
  violence who were incarcerated for acts of survival. The film has been f
 eatured by The New York Times\, the Chicago Tribune and ABC News.</p><p> 
  She is currently working on <em><a title="Original URL: https://www.docu
 mentaries.org/films/writing-for-my-mother/. Click or tap if you trust thi
 s link." href="https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%
 3A%2F%2Fwww.documentaries.org%2Ffilms%2Fwriting-for-my-mother%2F&amp\;dat
 a=05%7C02%7Cmrolfes%40iu.edu%7C68533c4a975c402135b208def48f0787%7C1113be3
 4aed14d00ab4bcdd02510be91%7C1%7C0%7C639217092379713731%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbG
 Zsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjo
 iTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp\;sdata=HJDUrVkh4JRuRMGml0LyUAR
 QNxyWimVxZrLDyPnKf38%3D&amp\;reserved=0" target="_blank" rel="noopener no
 referrer" data-auth="NotApplicable" data-linkindex="1">Writing for My Mot
 her</a></em>\, a documentary and book project exploring literacy in the U
 nited States\, the communities that have been excluded from educational o
 pportunities and what becomes possible in people's lives and for our demo
 cracy when those barriers are broken down.</p><p>  Natalie lives in Provi
 dence\, Rhode Island\, with her husband and three children. In her free t
 ime\, she can usually be found gardening\, knitting\, reading\, or taking
  unhurried walks.</p><p class="p1"><span class="s1"><a href="https://ands
 oistayedfilm.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong><picture class=
 "lw_image lw_image32013 lw_align_left"><source type="image/webp" srcset="
 https://events.iu.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/199/width/150/height/103/32
 013_And_So_I_Stayed_Hi-Res_Prouduction_Still_01.rev.1786929094.webp 2x\, 
 https://events.iu.edu/live/image/scale/3x/gid/199/width/150/height/103/32
 013_And_So_I_Stayed_Hi-Res_Prouduction_Still_01.rev.1786929094.webp 3x" d
 ata-origin="responsive"/><source type="image/jpeg" srcset="https://events
 .iu.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/199/width/150/height/103/32013_And_So_I_S
 tayed_Hi-Res_Prouduction_Still_01.rev.1786929094.jpg 2x\, https://events.
 iu.edu/live/image/scale/3x/gid/199/width/150/height/103/32013_And_So_I_St
 ayed_Hi-Res_Prouduction_Still_01.rev.1786929094.jpg 3x" data-origin="resp
 onsive"/><img width="150" height="103" alt="And So I Stayed" data-alt="An
 d So I Stayed" src="https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/199/width/150/he
 ight/103/32013_And_So_I_Stayed_Hi-Res_Prouduction_Still_01.rev.1786929094
 .jpg" title="And So I Stayed Hi-Res Prouduction Still 01" srcset="https:/
 /events.iu.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/199/width/150/height/103/32013_And
 _So_I_Stayed_Hi-Res_Prouduction_Still_01.rev.1786929094.jpg 2x\, https://
 events.iu.edu/live/image/scale/3x/gid/199/width/150/height/103/32013_And_
 So_I_Stayed_Hi-Res_Prouduction_Still_01.rev.1786929094.jpg 3x" data-max-w
 ="3200" data-max-h="2200" loading="lazy" data-optimized="true"/></picture
 >AND SO I STAYED</strong></a></span><span class="s1">is an<strong>&#160\;
 </strong>eye-opening and award-winning documentary about three survivors 
 of abuse fighting for their lives and how the legal system betrayed them.
 &#160\;</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1">These women paid a steep
  price with long prison sentences\, lost time with loved ones\, and painf
 ul memories. Formerly incarcerated survivor-advocate Kim Dadou Brown\, wh
 o met her wife while incarcerated\, is a driving force in the passage of 
 New York's Domestic Violence Survivors Justice Act (DVSJA)\, a new law me
 ant to prevent survivors from receiving harsh prison sentences for their 
 acts of survival. Nikki Addimando\, a mother of two young children\, suff
 ered the consequences when a judge didn't follow the law's guidelines. Ta
 nisha Davis\, a single mother who was ripped away from her son in 2013\, 
 is hopeful the new law is her way out of a harsh prison sentence.</span><
 /p><p class="p1"><span class="s1"><span data-olk-copy-source="MailCompose
 ">AND SO I STAYED aims to hold the legal system and public accountable by
  exposing the unjust misogyny and racism embedded in these power structur
 es while also portraying the resilience\, hopes\, and dreams of survivors
  and their loved ones.</span></span></p>
