SUMMARY:Environmental Futures Cross-Pollination Luncheon: Water Ways
DESCRIPTION:Join the Environmental Futures in the Arts and Humanities Ini
 tiative for our first 2026-2027 lunch-hour discussion in a series designe
 d to bring together scholars and artists in the arts and humanities whose
  work engages with "Water Ways"—whether through histories of trade\, em
 pire\, and exchange\, Indigenous knowledges\, literature\, environmental 
 justice issues\, and art. Each lunch will feature a panel of faculty who 
 will informally share their work-in-progress.  Our features speakers for 
 the fall lunch are:  Katina Bitsicas (BioArt\, Media School)  Michelle De
 l Rio (Public Health)  Rebecca Lave (Geography)  Teresa Kovacs (Germanic 
 Studies)  Ahmed Shams (Media School)
