SUMMARY:Global Competencies Skills Development Series: Crisis\, Power & P
 olicy Dinner with Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley
DESCRIPTION:Inside the Room Where Geopolitics Happens  How do you go from
  starting out in global affairs to shaping U.S. cyber strategy\, directin
 g counterterrorism operations\, and advising the Pentagon\, White House\,
  and Senate?  Join the Global Competencies Skills Development Series for 
 an intimate\, off-the-record style session with Ambassador Gina Abercromb
 ie-Winstanley—30-year Foreign Service veteran\, former U.S. Ambassador 
 to Malta\, and President of the Middle East Policy Council.  No scripted 
 presentations or generic advice—just real tradecraft from someone who h
 as managed war-zone evacuations under fire and negotiated at the highest 
 levels of national security.  Who Can Attend?  Open to all: Students (Und
 ergrad &amp\; Grad)\, Faculty\, Staff\, and the Public. (Catered dinner p
 rovided)  What You'll Get Out of It      Unfiltered Access: Direct\, smal
 l-group face time with a senior diplomat who operated across the State De
 partment\, Defense Department\, and National Security Council.          C
 risis Tradecraft: Real-world lessons on high-pressure decision-making\, f
 rom counterterrorism networks to cyber warfare and emergency evacuations.
           Insider Career Strategy: The exact playbook for breaking into n
 ational security\, intelligence\, foreign policy\, and top international 
 fellowships.          Raw Answers: Bring your real questions about power 
 dynamics\, navigating federal bureaucracy\, and building leverage early i
 n your career.      Bio: Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley  Ambassad
 or Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley is a 30-year diplomat\, former U.S. Ambass
 ador to the Republic of Malta\, and President of the Middle East Policy C
 ouncil. Her career spans executive leadership roles across the Department
  of State\, Defense Department\, National Security Council\, and Senate F
 oreign Relations Committee. She has advised the commander of U.S. cyber f
 orces on foreign policy priorities\, expanded international counterterror
 ism partnerships as Deputy Coordinator for Counterterrorism\, and led the
  emergency evacuation of thousands of U.S. citizens from a war zone. She 
 is a recipient of the State Department Superior Honor Award for acts of c
 ourage during an al-Qaeda attack on the U.S. Consulate in Jeddah.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h4 data-path-to-node="13">  Inside the Room
  Where Geopolitics Happens</h4><p data-path-to-node="14">  How do you go 
 from starting out in global affairs to shaping U.S. cyber strategy\, dire
 cting counterterrorism operations\, and advising the Pentagon\, White Hou
 se\, and Senate?</p><p data-path-to-node="15">  Join the Global Competenc
 ies Skills Development Series for an intimate\, off-the-record style sess
 ion with Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley—30-year Foreign Service
  veteran\, former U.S. Ambassador to Malta\, and President of the Middle 
 East Policy Council.</p><p data-path-to-node="16">  No scripted presentat
 ions or generic advice—just real tradecraft from someone who has manage
 d war-zone evacuations under fire and negotiated at the highest levels of
  national security.</p><h4 data-path-to-node="17">  Who Can Attend?</h4><
 p data-path-to-node="18">  Open to all: Students (Undergrad &amp\; Grad)\
 , Faculty\, Staff\, and the Public. <i data-path-to-node="18" data-index-
 in-node="74">(Catered dinner provided)</i></p><h4 data-path-to-node="19">
   What You'll Get Out of It</h4><ul data-path-to-node="20"><li><p data-pa
 th-to-node="20\,0\,0">      Unfiltered Access: Direct\, small-group face 
 time with a senior diplomat who operated across the State Department\, De
 fense Department\, and National Security Council.    </p></li><li><p data
 -path-to-node="20\,1\,0">      Crisis Tradecraft: Real-world lessons on h
 igh-pressure decision-making\, from counterterrorism networks to cyber wa
 rfare and emergency evacuations.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="20
 \,2\,0">      Insider Career Strategy: The exact playbook for breaking in
 to national security\, intelligence\, foreign policy\, and top internatio
 nal fellowships.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="20\,3\,0">      Ra
 w Answers: Bring your real questions about power dynamics\, navigating fe
 deral bureaucracy\, and building leverage early in your career.    </p></
 li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node="22">  Bio: Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Win
 stanley</h3><p data-path-to-node="23">  Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winst
 anley is a 30-year diplomat\, former U.S. Ambassador to the Republic of M
 alta\, and President of the Middle East Policy Council. Her career spans 
 executive leadership roles across the Department of State\, Defense Depar
 tment\, National Security Council\, and Senate Foreign Relations Committe
 e. She has advised the commander of U.S. cyber forces on foreign policy p
 riorities\, expanded international counterterrorism partnerships as Deput
 y Coordinator for Counterterrorism\, and led the emergency evacuation of 
 thousands of U.S. citizens from a war zone. She is a recipient of the Sta
 te Department Superior Honor Award for acts of courage during an al-Qaeda
  attack on the U.S. Consulate in Jeddah.</p>
